---
import LegalLayout from './LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  eyebrow="Legal"
  title="Privacy Policy"
  lead="CalcVantage Inc. ('CalcVantage', 'we', 'our', 'us') runs CalcVantage.com, a free library of financial calculators for the United States, Canada, and Australia. This policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and the choices you have. It applies to every visitor, regardless of country."
  lastUpdated="August 8, 2026"
  toc={[
    { id: 'information-we-collect', label: 'Information we collect' },
    { id: 'how-we-use-information', label: 'How we use your information' },
    { id: 'cookies-local-storage', label: 'Cookies and local storage' },
    { id: 'analytics', label: 'Analytics' },
    { id: 'third-party-services', label: 'Third-party services' },
    { id: 'data-security', label: 'Data security' },
    { id: 'data-retention', label: 'Data retention' },
    { id: 'your-rights', label: 'Your rights' },
    { id: 'international-users', label: 'International users' },
    { id: 'childrens-privacy', label: "Children's privacy" },
    { id: 'changes-to-policy', label: 'Changes to this policy' },
    { id: 'contact-information', label: 'Contact information' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="doc-section" id="overview">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">Overview</h2>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      The calculators on CalcVantage run entirely in your browser. The numbers you enter — a home
      price, a down payment, an interest rate, a savings goal — never leave your device and are
      never saved by us. You do not need an account to use the site, and we do not sell personal
      information. This policy is short by design: we process only the limited information
      described below, and only when it is necessary to make the website work or to improve it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="information-we-collect">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">Information we collect</h2>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">We collect very little information, and it falls into a few categories:</p>
    <ul class="doc-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Information you choose to send.</strong> If you use the
        <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>, you provide your name, email address, subject, and
        message so we can reply. We use this only to respond to you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Basic technical data.</strong> Our hosting service may record routine, non-personal
        data such as browser type, approximate region, the pages you visit, and network log data.
        This is typical of any website and is used for security and reliability.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cookies.</strong> With your consent, we and our analytics providers may store
        small files (cookies) in your browser. See the next section and our
        <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> for details.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      We do not turn the numbers you type into a calculator, your financial details, or your
      personal identity in any database.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="how-we-use-information">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">How we use your information</h2>
    <ul class="doc-list">
      <li>To operate, secure, and maintain the website and its features.</li>
      <li>To respond to messages received through the contact form.</li>
      <li>To understand aggregate usage — for example, which calculators are most popular — so we can improve the platform.</li>
      <li>To comply with applicable laws and to enforce our <a href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      We do not use your information for advertising, for building a personal profile of you, or
      for anything beyond what is described in this policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="cookies-local-storage">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      CalcVantage uses cookies and similar storage mechanisms only as described in our
      <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>. In summary, a small number of essential cookies
      help the website work correctly, and — only with your consent — analytics cookies help us
      understand aggregate usage. You can clear or block cookies at any time in your browser
      without affecting the calculators.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="analytics">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">Analytics</h2>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      We may use third-party web analytics to understand how visitors use the site in aggregate —
      which pages are visited, how long each page is viewed, and which tools are used. This data
      is collected in your browser and is not used to identify you. Where we rely on analytics
      cookies, we ask for consent first, and you can withdraw that consent at any time by clearing
      the relevant cookies. The aggregate insights help us decide which calculators to improve and
      what educational content to publish.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="third-party-services">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">Third-party services</h2>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      We keep third-party involvement minimal. We may use a small set of providers for hosting,
      infrastructure, analytics, and — in the future — for delivering contact-form messages.
      These providers may process the technical data described above under their own terms, may
      transfer data across borders, and receive only the information needed to provide their
      service. We review our providers to confirm they apply reasonable privacy practices.
    </p>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      The calculators themselves do not rely on third-party services for the mathematics. The
      arithmetic is performed locally in your browser.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="data-security">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">Data security</h2>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      We take protecting your data seriously. Because the calculators never process your inputs on
      a server, most of your financial information never leaves your device in the first place.
      Where we do handle personal data, we apply reasonable organizational and technical measures,
      including encrypted connections (HTTPS) and restricted access to any systems we control. No
      method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but we work to keep our systems
      limited and protected.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="data-retention">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">Data retention</h2>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      We keep contact messages only as long as necessary to respond to them and address the
      request, and we aim to delete them soon after. Aggregate analytics statistics are kept
      without identifying attributes for a longer period. Any preferences stored in your browser
      remain under your control until you clear them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="your-rights">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">Your rights</h2>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      Depending on where you live — for example under the GDPR in the European Economic Area or the
      CPRA in California — you may have the right to access, correct, or delete your personal data,
      and to object to or restrict certain processing. Because we hold so little data, exercising
      these rights is usually straightforward.
    </p>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      To make such a request, contact us using the details highlighted at the bottom of this page.
      We will respond within a reasonable period. You may also have the right to lodge a complaint
      with your local data-protection authority.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="international-users">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">International users</h2>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      CalcVantage serves visitors around the world, and our calculators are tailored for the United
      States, Canada, and Australia. Any data we hold may be transferred to, and processed in, a
      country with privacy laws that differ from your own. In such cases we rely on appropriate
      safeguards and only process the minimum data described in this policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="childrens-privacy">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">Children&rsquo;s privacy</h2>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      CalcVantage is a general financial-education website and is not directed at children under
      the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe
      a child has provided us with personal data, please contact us and we will delete it as soon
      as possible.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="changes-to-policy">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      We may update this Privacy Policy when we add features, change providers, or laws that
      affect us change. When we do, we will revise the &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date at the top
      of this page, and — if the change is significant — publish a notice on the website. We
      encourage you to review this page from time to time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="contact-information">
    <h2 class="doc-section-title">Contact information</h2>
    <p class="doc-section-copy">
      If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, or about your personal data, please reach
      out through the <a href="/contact">Contact Us</a> page. We will do our best to reply promptly
      and helpfully.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>